{{Quote|Kickin' Hawk's my best hand-to-hand fighter... Foot-to-head fighter.|Kickin' Hawk preparing to battle Master [[Kundo]].<ref name="Rook Tales">''[[Rook Tales]]''</ref>}}
Kickin' Hawk's species are extremely proficient hand-to-hand fighters. As such, Kickin' Hawk is recognized by [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] as his best close-ranged hand-to-hand fighter. This was demonstrated in several of his fights, notably the ones against [[Fistrick]],<ref name="BiS">''[[Bros in Space]]''</ref> [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]],<ref name="WXIP1">[[Weapon XI: Part 1]]</ref> and [[Kundo]].<ref name="Rook Tales" /> [[Liam]] was also able to decently hold on his own against [[Rook Blonko|Rook]].<ref name="TCOM">''[[The Color of Monkey]]''</ref>

Kickin' Hawk has sharp talons on his arms he can use against his opponents, as demonstrated by Liam.<ref name="TCOM" /> These talons can also be extended out, also demonstrated by Liam.<ref name="TMTCP1">''[[The More Things Change: Part 1]]''</ref>

Kickin' Hawk has enhanced strength, being able to kick Fistrick across a room<ref name="BiS" /> and harm Kevin in his metallic form.<ref name="WXIP1" /> Kickin Hawk also has enhanced durability, being able to withstand Kevin slamming a large metal mallet on him.<ref name="WXIP1" />

Kickin' Hawk has enhanced jumping, being able to jump extremely high and leap large distances.<ref name="OMWAT">''[[O Mother, Where Art Thou?]]''</ref> He is also very acrobatic and flexible.<ref name="BiS" />

Kickin' Hawk is quite agile and can run extremely fast, enough to leave behind a trail of dust as he runs.<ref>''[[Collect This]]''</ref>

Kickin' Hawk is capable of withstanding the vacuum of space, but he still needs to breathe to survive. Without an oxygen supply, Kickin' Hawk is limited to holding his breath.<ref name="TT">''[[Tummy Trouble]]''</ref>

==Weaknesses==
Kickin' Hawk can be distracted by bird seeds, as demonstrated by [[Liam]].<ref name="TMTCP1" />

Kickin' Hawk will collapse and fall asleep if his neck is rubbed, as demonstrated by Liam.<ref>''[[Clyde 5]]''</ref>

Kickin' Hawk is vulnerable to electricity, as demonstrated by Liam.<ref>''[[The More Things Change: Part 2]]''</ref><ref name="Outbreak" />

==History==
===Omniverse===
*Kickin' Hawk first appeared in ''[[Outbreak]]'', where he was added to the active playlist after the [[Omnitrix (Omniverse)|Omnitrix]] "sampled" [[Liam]]'s DNA{{Refn|[[Liam]] is not Kickin' Hawk's genetic donor, as whenever the [[Omnitrix (Omniverse)|Omnitrix]] detects uncatalogued DNA, it will vocally alert [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] and will disable its functions if it does not get close enough to the subject. This means it would have sampled Liam's DNA when Ben first encountered him in ''[[The More Things Change: Part 1]]'' if his DNA was not already catalogued as in the case with [[Whampire]].<ref>''[[The Vampire Strikes Back]]''</ref>|group = note}} and defeated the latter.
*In ''[[Bros in Space]]'', Kickin' Hawk defeated [[Fistrick]] and his [[Muroid]] army.
*In ''[[T.G.I.S.]]'', Kickin' Hawk and [[Zak Saturday|Zak]] battled [[V.V. Argost|Argost]].
*In ''[[Tummy Trouble]]'', Kickin' Hawk fought [[Attea|General Attea]] until he reverted.
*In ''[[Vilgax Must Croak]]'', Kickin' Hawk entered [[Incarcecon]] with the other [[Plumbers]] before briefly attacking [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]] out of anger.
*In ''[[O Mother, Where Art Thou?]]'', Kickin' Hawk knocked some TNT out of the [[Vreedle Brothers]]' hands and kicked it away before it exploded.
*In ''[[Collect This]]'', Kickin' Hawk played soccer with [[Rook Blonko|Rook]] and the Kineceleran kids and accidentally wrecked [[Pakmar]]'s lamp store after scoring a goal.
*In ''[[Weapon XI: Part 1]]'', Kickin' Hawk tried to fight [[Servantis]], but was stopped and defeated by [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]], forcing Kickin' Hawk to escape the [[Rooter Headquarters]] with the rest of [[Ben's Team (Omniverse)|his team]].
*In ''[[Rook Tales]]'', Kickin' Hawk was defeated by [[Kundo]].
*In ''[[Charm School]]'', Kickin' Hawk "protected" [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]] from [[Hex (Classic)|Hex]] by pinning the latter against a tree.
*In ''[[Vreedlemania]]'', Kickin' Hawk fought the [[Vreedle]]s and was defeated by the [[Krakken]].
*In ''[[Third Time's a Charm]]'', Kickin' Hawk battled and tricked [[Charmcaster (Classic)|Charmcaster]] with [[Skurd]]'s help before kicking her into [[Bag of Tricks|her bag]].
*In ''[[The Most Dangerous Game Show]]'', Kickin' Hawk escaped the [[Null Void (Classic)|Null Void]] with all the contestants and was defeated by [[Charles Zenith]].
*In ''[[A New Dawn]]'', Kickin' Hawk appeared for a short time when [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] was cycling through his aliens.

