==Etymology==
Kickin' Hawk's name is a portmanteau of "kicking", his main fighting technique; and "[[Wikipedia: Chickenhawk (bird)|chickenhawk]]", referencing his hawk-like appearance.

==Trivia==
*Kickin' Hawk's existence was confirmed on the [[Wikipedia:Entertainment Earth|Entertainment Earth]] website.
*Kickin' Hawk appears to make a screeching sound when he talks, much like how Liam often makes chicken noises when he speaks.
**The same sound can be heard during Kickin' Hawk's transformation sequence and whenever he kicks.
**Said sound appears to be the infamous stock eagle screech, which is the cry of the red-tailed hawk. Interestingly, the red-tailed hawk is among the three birds of prey that were once known as chickenhawks.
*[[Albedo]] is unable to transform into Kickin' Hawk.{{Refn|[[:File:Albedo Does Not Have Outbreak Aliens.png]]|group = DJW}}
*[[Derrick J. Wyatt]] possibly came up with Kickin' Hawk, but could not remember if that was true.{{Refn|[[:File:Derrick Came Up With Ball Weevil.png]]|group = DJW}} He was conceived after the creation of [[Liam]].{{Refn|[[:File:Kickin Hawk Was Conceived After Liam.png]]|group = DJW}}
*Kickin' Hawk went by multiple working names, such as Ka-Chickin, Chi-Kickin, Ch'Kickin, and KiChicken, before his final name was coined by [[Matt Wayne]].{{Refn|[[:File:Kickin Hawk Working Names.png]]|group = DJW}}{{Refn|[[:File:Matt Wayne Named Kickin Hawk.png]]|group = DJW}}
*Kickin' Hawk was designed by Derrick.{{Refn|[[:File:Some of the Aliens Designed by Derrick in OV.png]]|group = DJW}}
*Kickin' Hawk's Spinning Kick Attack somewhat resembles the Tatsumaki Senpukyaku from ''Street Fighter''.
*Kickin' Hawk's mask resembles that of [[Wikipedia:Hawkman|Hawkman]]. The rest of his outfit bears a close resemblance to the 1980's design of [[Wikipedia:Marvel Comics|Marvel]]'s [[Wikipedia:Hercules (Marvel Comics)|Hercules]].

